:value "2005798"} "Doubles, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2005839"} "Doubles, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900340"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "90016756"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "42107"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "42323"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "42579"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "42802"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258065"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "304111"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "351671"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19005318"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/125"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Singles, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July –  5 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2159"} "Porte de la Chapelle Arena, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2005717"} "39 from 35 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The only-seeded player to be eliminated at the group stage was " [:a {:href "/athletes/125109"} "Tai Tzu-Ying"] " (TPE), the number three seed and player ranked third in the world, who lost to " [:a {:href "/athletes/124519"} "Ratchanok Intanon"] " (THA) by a score of 21-19, 21-15. It meant that Intanon gained a bye into the quarter-finals. Again, players from Asian countries dominated the group winners, the only exceptions being fourth-seeded " [:a {:href "/athletes/124034"} "Carolina Marín"] " (ESP) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/147142"} "Beiwen Zhang"] " (USA)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The top two seeds " [:a {:href "/athletes/144901"} "An Se-Yeong"] " (KOR) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141821"} "Chen Yufei"] " (CHN), along with Intanon, had byes into the quarter-finals. In the round of 16, there were no surprises, with the higher ranked players all winning against their lower ranked opponents, the highlights arguably being the victory of " [:a {:href "/athletes/150942"} "Aya Ohori"] " (JPN) over " [:a {:href "/athletes/146522"} "Yeo Jia Min"] " (SGP) by 11-21, 21-14, 24-22, and, having lost the first set, Carolina Marín was made to work to defeat Beiwen Zhang 12-21, 21-9, 21-18. " [:a {:href "/athletes/130762"} "Akane Yamaguchi"] " (JPN), " [:a {:href "/athletes/143702"} "Gregoria Mariska Tunjung"] " (INA), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101443"} "He Bingjiao"] " (CHN) completed the quarter-final line-up."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The only match involving three games in the quarter-finals was between An and Yamaguchi, the number one seed finally overcoming her opponent 15-21, 21-17, 21-8 after a 74-minute contest. In the other quarter finals, Tunjung defeated her unseeded opponent Intanon, Carolina Marín overcoming Aya Ohori, and, in an all-Chinese contest, He Bingjiao had the better of her compatriot Chen Yufei."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first semi-final was another thrilling victory for An over Tunjung by 11-21, 21-13, 21-16. However, the second semi-final saw heartache for Carolina Marín. Leading comfortably (21-14, 10-5) against her opponent He Bingjiao, she landed awkwardly following a rally. Whilst she had her leg strapped, she was unable to continue much longer and Marín was forced to retire when leading 21-14, 10-8."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Sadly, Marín’s injury prevented her from contesting the bronze medal match, so Tunjung was awarded the medal via a walkover. The final itself resulted in a comfortable victory for top seed An as she defeated He by 21-13, 21-16."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-st